                <h2>Why Conduct Compliance Audits</h2>
<p>A utility app team once had 3 advertising accounts suspended simultaneously due to inconsistencies between landing page information and advertiser details, resulting in losses exceeding $2,000. Compliance audits aren't just about passing platform reviews—they're about protecting your account assets and campaign schedules. Make audits a regular workflow rather than waiting for problems to occur.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Pre-Audit Preparations</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Download latest policy documents</strong>: Download the newest advertising policy updates from each platform's backend at the end of each month</li>
<li><strong>Compile recent violation records</strong>: Gather all ad disapprovals from the past 30 days</li>
<li><strong>Backup account settings</strong>: Export key information like account structure and campaign settings before auditing</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Checkpoint</strong>: Only proceed with the formal audit after confirming all 3 preparation items are complete.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Operations Checklist: 12 Self-Inspection Steps</h2>
<h3>I. Account Entity Information (Required)</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Company name consistency</strong>: Check if the advertising account entity matches the business license exactly, including spaces, brackets, and other details</li>
<li><strong>Address verification</strong>: The business license registration address must match the address filled in during account setup</li>
<li><strong>Document validity</strong>: Confirm that business licenses, legal representative IDs, and other documents are within their validity period</li>
<li><strong>Contact information availability</strong>: Ensure admin email and phone can normally receive platform notifications</li>
</ol>
<h3>II. Ad Content Compliance (Key Focus Areas)</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>No absolute language</strong>: Check for terms like "best," "#1," "100%" etc.</li>
<li><strong>Image copyright compliance</strong>: Ensure all images have legitimate licensing or original proof</li>
<li><strong>Landing page consistency</strong>: Content promised in ads must have corresponding display on landing pages</li>
<li><strong>Sensitive industry qualifications</strong>: Verify advertising qualifications for finance, healthcare, education, and other regulated industries</li>
</ol>
<h3>III. Campaign Settings Compliance (Often Overlooked)</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Audience targeting compliance</strong>: Confirm that target countries/regions don't involve sensitive demographic targeting</li>
<li><strong>Creative dimension standards</strong>: Different platforms have varying requirements for image and video dimensions</li>
<li><strong>Privacy policy statements</strong>: Advertising in EU, Middle East, and other regions requires explicit privacy policy statements</li>
<li><strong>Budget and bidding strategy</strong>: Check for abnormal spending caused by aggressive bidding</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Post-Audit Processing</h2>
<h3>Documentation and Reporting</h3>
<p>After completing the audit, fill out a simple inspection record form:</p>
