</tr>
<tr>
<td>Before holidays</td>
<td>Special inspection 3 days before holidays</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Policy change periods</td>
<td>Complete corresponding checks within 48 hours of policy release</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Account anomalies</td>
<td>Initiate audit immediately upon discovering anomalies</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<hr />
<h2>Quick FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q: Found violations in historical campaigns that have already finished running. Should I still address them?</strong><br />
A: It's recommended to record them in the inspection report as reference for future creative design. Completed campaigns won't trigger penalties, but this helps the team accumulate compliance experience.</p>
<p><strong>Q: When managing multiple accounts, what differs in audit priorities?</strong><br />
A: For main accounts, focus on entity qualifications and campaign strategies. For sub-accounts, focus on creative compliance and landing page consistency.</p>
